0..74 Comment "// A result that follows its argument (#392). A recursive definition whose"
75..152 Comment "// result is the type it recurses on, and which holds with that result at its"
153..229 Comment "// parameter\'s own stage — every branch returns a value no larger than the"
230..311 Comment "// argument — returns at the stage of the argument a call hands it. A recursion"
312..387 Comment "// then descends through such a call: division recurses on what subtraction"
388..461 Comment "// leaves of its dividend\'s predecessor, and a logarithm on half of it. A"
462..532 Comment "// definition with no recursion opens no stage, and its result follows"
533..606 Comment "// nothing. What refuses is in `../../pathological/data/following.gandr`."
608..655 Comment "// The naturals and the numerals two and three."
